{"The new `enableSqlExpressions` helper in `reader.go` always returns `false` regardless of the feature flag, so the flag no longer has any effect; if the intention is to hard-disable SQL expressions, simplify this logic (and potentially remove the flag dependency), or otherwise make the enable/disable behavior explicit and consistent.": 0.902906596660614, "The new `pkg/expr/sql/db.go` methods all return 'not implemented' errors; if SQL expressions are intentionally disabled, it might be clearer to surface a single, consistent error message at the entry point (e.g., in `ReadQuery`) and avoid providing stubbed DB methods that appear usable but are effectively dead code.": 0.12344754487276077, "In `sql_command.go` and `pkg/expr/sql/parser.go` you now call `sql.NewInMemoryDB()` / `NewInMemoryDB()`, but there is no visible import of the new `pkg/expr/sql` package or aliasing to avoid confusion with the standard `database/sql` package, which is likely to cause compile issues; consider adding a clear import alias (e.g. `sqlexpr`) and using it consistently.": 0.172109454870224}